\v 32 \wj They're¦44413 like¦44412 little¦44415 children¦44415 sitting¦44421 in¦44417 the¦44419 marketplace¦44419 and¦44422 calling¦44423 out¦44423 to¦44424 each¦44432 other, ‘We¦44431 played¦44431 the¦44431 flute¦44431 for¦44432 you¦44432 all¦44432 but you¦44435 didn't dance¦44435, then we¦44436 played a sad song but you¦44440 all¦44440 didn't weep¦44440.’\wj*
\v 33 \wj Because¦44442 Yohan-the-immerser came¦44441 and¦44457 he didn't eat¦44450 bread¦44451 or drink¦44455 wine¦44456, so you¦44458 all¦44458 said¦44458 that he has¦44441 a demon¦44460.\wj*
\v 34 \wj Then the¦44463 son¦44464 of¦44466 humanity¦44466 came¦44462 and ate¦44467 and¦44468 drank¦44469 and¦44470 you¦44471 all¦44471 said¦44471, ‘Look¦44473, he's a¦44474 glutton¦44475 and¦44476 a drunkard¦44477—a friend¦44478 of¦44479 tax-collectors and¦44481 those who disobey God.’\wj*
\v 35 \wj But¦44483 wisdom¦44486 is¦44484 justified¦44484 by¦44487 all¦44488 her¦44492 children¦44491.\wj*”
\s1 The woman who anoints Yeshua's feet
