\v 34 \wj and¦48543 went up¦48545 to him and bandaged¦48545 his wounds¦48547, pouring¦48549 olive¦48551 oil¦48551 and¦48552 wine¦48553 on them, then put him¦48557 on¦48559 his¦48560 own¦48561 animal and¦48567 took¦48568 him to a roadhouse and looked after him.\wj*
\v 35 \wj The¦48572 next¦48574 day¦48572 he¦48578 took¦48588 out¦48577 two¦48579 coins¦48580 and gave¦48578 them to¦48600 their host, instructing, ‘Look after this guy and if it costs more than this, I'll¦48603 reimburse you¦48595 on¦48598 my way¦48599 back¦48603.’\wj*
\p
\v 36 “\wj So which¦48605 of¦48608 those¦48608 three¦48610 do you¦48614 think¦48612 acted like the neighbour¦48611 of¦48617 the one attacked by robbers¦48621?\wj*”
