\p
\v 38 When¦48646 it was time¦48648 to¦48649 leave¦48649, Yeshua went¦48654 into¦48657 a village¦48658 and¦48661 there was a woman¦48660 there named¦48663 Martha¦48664 who welcomed¦48665 him¦48666 in.\x + \xo 10:38-39: \xt Yhn 11:1.\x*
\v 39 She¦48677 had¦48684 a sister¦48678 named¦48679 Maria¦48680 who¦48681 was¦48693 also¦48673 sitting there \add on the floor\add* by¦48684 \nd Yeshua's¦48692\nd* feet¦48688 listening¦48693 to¦48675 his¦48697 teaching.
\v 40 But¦48708 Martha¦48700 kept getting pulled¦48701 away¦48701 to keep the household running, and¦48708 \add after a while\add* approached¦48705 Yeshua and asked¦48709, “\nd Master¦48710\nd*, doesn't it¦48713 bother you¦48714 that¦48715 my¦48718 sister¦48717 has¦48705 left¦48724 all the housework to me? Tell¦48727 her¦48729 to come¦48705 and help¦48735 me¦48731.”
