\v 42 \wj but¦48756 only one¦48755 thing really matters. Maria¦48762 chose¦48769 the¦48765 best thing, and it won't¦48772 be¦48773 taken¦48773 away¦48773 from¦48774 her¦48775.\wj*”
\c 11
\s1 Yeshua teaches about prayer
\rem /s1 Jesus' Teaching on Prayer; The Lord's Prayer
\r (Mat. 6:9-13; 7:7-11)
\p
\v 1 One time¦48780 Yeshua was at¦48779 a place¦48784 praying¦48786, and¦48776 when¦48788 he¦48789 finished¦48789 some of¦48792 his followers¦48793 asked¦48790 him¦48794, “\nd Master¦48797\nd*, Yohan-the-immerser taught¦48804 his apprentices¦48806 how to¦48795 pray. You teach¦48798 us¦48799 as¦48801 well.”
\p
\v 2 So¦48810 Yeshua told¦48832 them¦48812, “\wj Whenever¦48813 you¦48814 all¦48814 pray¦48814, say¦48832 this:\wj*
\q1 \wj Father¦48833, may¦48814 \+add ≈all people honour you as their holy God\+add*.\wj*
\q1 \wj May¦48814 \+add ≈you¦48842 reign as king¦48848\+add* \+add over the earth\+add*.\wj*
\q1
\v 3 \wj Every¦48871 day¦48872 give¦48867 us¦48869 the¦48865 food¦48863 that¦48870 we need¦48866.\wj*
\q1
\v 4 \wj Forgive¦48875 us for¦48884 our¦48881 sins¦48879 because¦48884 we've forgiven¦48875 those who owed¦48892 \+add something\+add* to¦48889 us.\wj*
\q1 \wj Don't¦48896 bring¦48897 us¦48893 into¦48899 \+add situations where\+add* we're tempted¦48900.\wj*”
\rem /s1 Perseverance in Prayer
\p
\v 5 Then¦48907 he¦48908 told¦48908 them¦48910, “\wj \+add Imagine\+add* you¦48913 had¦48914 a friend¦48915 and¦48916 went¦48917 to¦48918 them at¦48920 midnight¦48920 and asked¦48908, ‘Friend¦48927, lend¦48928 me¦48929 some bread\wj*
\v 6 \wj because¦48932 a travelling friend¦48933 of¦48934 mine arrived¦48936 at my¦48934 place, and¦48944 I¦48946 haven't got¦48936 anything to give him¦48949 to eat.’\wj*
\v 7 \wj And¦48950 the one in the \+add other\+add* house might¦48956 reply, ‘Don't¦48958 bother me¦48959 \+add now\+add* because the¦48963 house is¦48966 locked and¦48967 the¦48968 kids¦48970 are¦48982 asleep beside me¦48973 here in¦48974 the¦48976 bed¦48978. I can't¦48958 get up¦48988 and get anything¦48989 for you¦48990.’\wj*
\v 8 \wj I'm¦48991 telling¦48991 all¦48992 of you¦48992 that even¦48994 if¦48993 that¦49000 friend¦49004 wouldn't get up and give them anything because¦49007 of¦49007 their friendship, then the¦49010 friend will¦49015 certainly get up and give them \+add some food\+add* if they persist¦49011 \+add in knocking\+add*.\wj*
\v 9 \wj So¦49021 this is what I'm¦49021 telling¦49023 you¦49022: \+add Keep submitting\+add* your requests¦49026 and¦49027 it'll¦49028 be¦49028 given¦49028 to¦49029 you¦49029 all¦49029, keep searching and¦49031 you'll all¦49032 find¦49032 \+add what you're looking for\+add*, keep knocking¦49033 and¦49034 the door will¦49035 be¦49035 opened¦49035 for you¦49036 all¦49036,\wj*
\v 10 \wj because¦49038 everyone¦49037 who requests¦49040 will receive¦49041, and¦49042 everyone who searches¦49044 will find¦49045, and¦49046 everyone who knocks¦49048 will¦49049 find opened¦49049 \+add doors\+add*.\wj*
\v 11 \wj How many¦49056 of¦49055 you¦49056 fathers¦49059, if your¦49056 child¦49062 asked¦49060 you for \+add some\+add* fish¦49073, you'd give¦49083 them a snake¦49080 instead¦49078?\wj*
\v 12 \wj Or¦49084 the child would¦49091 ask¦49091 for an¦49093 egg¦49093 and¦49087 you'd pass¦49096 them a scorpion¦49100?\wj*
\v 13 \wj So¦49112 if¦49111 you¦49113 all¦49113 know¦49117 how to give good¦49119 things to your children¦49123 despite your being¦49116 evil¦49114, how¦49125 much¦49125 more¦49126 the¦49127 father¦49128 in heaven¦49132 will¦49134 give¦49134 \+add the\+add* holy¦49137 \+nd spirit¦49135\+nd* to those who¦49130 ask¦49140 him¦49141.\wj*”
\s1 Yeshua is accused of being demon-possessed
\rem /s1 Opposition and questioning; Jesus and the Prince of Demons; Jesus and Beelzebul; Jesus and Beelzebub
\r (Mark 3:20-27; Mat. 12:22-30)
\p
\v 14 Then¦49149 Yeshua drove out¦49151 a demon that caused muteness, and¦49149 after the¦49161 demon¦49162 departed, the¦49168 man¦49169 was¦49150 able to speak¦49167. The¦49174 crowds¦49175 were¦49150 amazed,
\v 15 but¦49178 yet some¦49177 of¦49179 them¦49180 said¦49183, “He's¦49192 driving¦49192 out¦49192 demons because he's¦49192 Beelzebul¦49186 the¦49187 leader¦49189 of¦49190 the¦49190 demons¦49191.”\x + \xo 11:15: \xt Mat 9:34; 10:25.\x*
\p
\v 16 Others¦49206 who wanted¦49216 to test¦49208 \add who he was\add*, asked Yeshua to send a sign¦49209 from¦49214 heaven,\x + \xo 11:16: \xt Mrk 8:11; Mat 12:38; 16:1.\x*
\v 17 but¦49220 he¦49219 knew¦49221 their¦49222 thoughts¦49224 and told¦49226 them¦49222, “\wj Any kingdom¦49229 that's divided¦49235 against¦49232 itself¦49233 is¦49236 doomed, and¦49237 any household¦49238 that's divided will self-destruct.\wj*
\v 18 \wj So¦49244 if¦49243 Satan¦49247 was¦49252 fighting against¦49248 himself¦49249, how¦49254 could his¦49258 kingdom¦49257 even remain? Yes, I know that you're all¦49261 saying¦49261 that I must be¦49265 Beelzebul in order to¦49265 drive out¦49265 demons¦49270,\wj*
\v 19 \wj but¦49272 if¦49271 I have Beelzebul's power over demons, then¦49272 whose power do \+em your¦49281\+em* apprentices use to drive out¦49286 demons?\wj*
\v 20 \wj However if¦49299 I'm¦49305 driving¦49306 out¦49306 demons¦49308 with power that comes¦49310 from God, then that means that \nd God's¦49304\nd* kingdom¦49314 is¦49306 right in the¦49307 middle of you¦49312 all¦49312.\wj*
\p
\v 21 “\wj Whenever¦49317 a strong¦49319 \+add landowner\+add* arms¦49320 himself¦49325 and guards¦49322 his¦49334 nice home, everything remains there peacefully¦49329,\wj*
\v 22 \wj but¦49356 when¦49336 someone stronger¦49339 than¦49339 him¦49340 arrives¦49342 and overpowers¦49345 him¦49347, he'll even take¦49351 the¦49348 body armour¦49349 that¦49353 the \+add landowner\+add* put his trust¦49354 in¦49352, and then relieve him of¦49350 all his goods.\wj*
\p
\v 23 “\wj Anyone who doesn't \+add follow\+add* me¦49367 is¦49370 against¦49368 me¦49369, and¦49371 anyone who doesn't gather¦49374 with¦49375 us, \+add wants to\+add* scatter¦49377 us.\wj*\x + \xo 11:23: \xt Mrk 9:40.\x*
\s1 The return of demons
