\v 42 “\wj But¦49860 you Pharisees¦49836 won't¦49867 end well, because¦49838 you give a tenth of your herbs and vegetables, yet you¦49834 all¦49834 ignore giving justice¦49853 and¦49854 loving¦49856 \+nd God¦49858\+nd*, both of which need to¦49863 be done¦49863 and¦49864 cannot be ignored.\wj*\x + \xo 11:42: \xt Lev 27:30.\x*
\p
\v 43 “\wj You¦49873 Pharisees¦49875 won't end well, because¦49877 you¦49873 all¦49873 love¦49878 the¦49879 best¦49880 seats¦49880 in¦49881 the¦49882 \+add ≈Jewish¦49883 meeting¦49883 halls¦49883\+add* and¦49884 the¦49885 \+add honoured\+add* greetings¦49886 in¦49887 the¦49888 marketplaces¦49890.\wj*
\v 44 \wj You¦49899 all¦49899 won't¦49920 end well, because¦49904 you're like¦49906 unmarked graves¦49909 that people¦49914 walk¦49916 all over¦49917 without even realising\+add —the people simply don't know that you're dead inside\+add*.\wj*”
\p
\v 45 One¦49924 of¦49925 the¦49925 experts in religious rules \add there\add* answered¦49922 him¦49928 \add back\add*, “Teacher¦49929, you're¦49934 insulting¦49934 us¦49933 as well when you¦49934 say that.”
\p
\v 46 “\wj \+add Well,\+add* you law experts won't¦49960 end well,\wj*” Yeshua responded¦49937, “\wj because¦49944 you¦49945 put unbearably¦49952 \+add heavy\+add* burdens¦49949 onto the¦49962 shoulders of¦49957 the¦49947 people¦49948, yet you wouldn't move your¦49959 \+add little\+add* fingers¦49958 to¦49939 touch¦49961 those burdens yourselves¦49954.\wj*
\v 47 \wj You¦49965 all¦49965 won't end well, because¦49966 you¦49967 all¦49967 build¦49967 \+add fancy\+add* tombs¦49969 for the¦49970 prophets¦49971 that your¦49976 own ancestors¦49975 executed.\wj*
\v 48 \wj Because¦49992 of¦49989 that, you're all¦49981 \+add actually\+add* admitting and¦49983 agreeing to¦49987 what your¦49991 ancestors¦49990 did, because¦49992 they¦49993 killed¦49995 them¦49996 and \+add then\+add* you¦49997 build¦49999 their¦49999 tombs¦49999.\wj*
\v 49 \wj That's why \+nd God¦50009\+nd* in his wisdom¦50007 said¦50010, ‘I'll¦50011 send¦50011 prophets¦50015 and¦50016 missionaries¦50017 to¦50013 them¦50014, which they¦50021 will¦50021 \+add then\+add* persecute¦50023 and kill¦50021\wj*’
\v 50 \wj so that¦50032 the¦50027 blood¦50028 of¦50029 those prophets¦50031 which¦50032 was¦50033 spilt from¦50035 the¦50036 creation¦50036 of¦50037 the¦50037 world¦50037 \+add onwards\+add* would then be¦50026 charged to this¦50042 generation¦50041.\wj*
\v 51 \wj \+add This goes all the way back to\+add* to the¦50045 blood¦50045 of¦50046 Hevel¦50046 \+add (Abel)\+add*, right up to¦50047 the¦50049 blood¦50049 of¦50050 Zekaryah¦50050 who was \+add recently\+add* killed between¦50059 the¦50060 altar¦50061 and¦50062 the¦50063 temple¦50065 sanctuary. Yes¦50066, I'm¦50067 telling¦50067 all of you¦50068, \+add those crimes\+add* will¦50070 be¦50070 charged to \+em this¦50075\+em* generation¦50073.\wj*\x + \xo 11:51: a \xt Gen 4:8; \xo b \xt 2Ch 24:20-21.\x*
\p
\v 52 “\wj You¦50077 religious law experts won't¦50089 end well, because¦50080 you¦50082 took¦50082 away¦50082 the¦50083 key¦50084 to¦50077 knowledge¦50086—not only did you¦50090 not¦50089 enter¦50090 \+add yourselves\+add*, but¦50091 you also¦50091 forbade¦50095 others from entering¦50094.\wj*”
\p
\v 53 Once Yeshua left that \add house\add*, the¦50112 religious¦50114 teachers¦50114 and¦50115 the¦50116 Pharisee¦50118 party¦50118 started strongly resenting¦50121 him, and¦50122 started \add a plan of\add* asking him¦50125 more¦50128 questions
